{"book":10,"chapter":30,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / ASYNCHRONY / CHAPTER 30","slides":[{"title":"Why async","sub":"Chapter 30 · Waiting","short":"Intro","main":"One thread, many tasks; concurrency vs parallelism.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Waiting","One thread, many tasks","Concurrency and parallelism"],"captions":["Most of the time a server waits: response, disk, database","10,000 connections can't mean 10,000 OS threads: one thread switches between tasks","Concurrency: many things in progress; parallelism: several run at one moment on different cores"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"request","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"waiting…","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"response","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"thread","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k0","x":60.0,"y":100.0,"w":66.0,"h":28.0,"text":"task 1","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k1","x":140.0,"y":100.0,"w":66.0,"h":28.0,"text":"task 2","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k2","x":220.0,"y":100.0,"w":66.0,"h":28.0,"text":"task 3","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k3","x":300.0,"y":100.0,"w":66.0,"h":28.0,"text":"task 4","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"concurrency\nswitching","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"parallelism\nseparate cores","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.8,33.7]}]},{"title":"asyncio","sub":"Event loop","short":"asyncio","main":"Three ways in Python; async def and await; blocking the loop.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Three ways","Event loop","Blocking"],"captions":["Python: threads (limited by GIL), processes (costly data copying), asyncio","async def and await: a coroutine hands control to the event loop in one thread","time.sleep in a coroutine freezes the whole loop: the most common mistake"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"threads","tone":"muted","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"processes","tone":"muted","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"asyncio","tone":"muted","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["async def fetch():","    await asyncio.sleep(1)","asyncio.run(main())"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["async def bad():","    time.sleep(5)   # whole loop stalls"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[15.9,32.9]}]},{"title":"Python coroutines","sub":"create_task, gather","short":"Coroutines","main":"Coroutine object, create_task, gather.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Coroutine object","create_task","gather"],"captions":["Calling an async function without await makes an object and does nothing: \"coroutine was never awaited\"","create_task queues the coroutine on the loop: it starts at the next switch","gather runs several and collects results; wait_for limits time"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["c = fetch()      # an object, not running","await c         # now it runs"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["t = asyncio.create_task(fetch())","# starts as soon as the loop switches"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["a, b = await asyncio.gather(f(1), f(2))"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[15.8,24.9]}]},{"title":"Future in Rust","sub":"A lazy state machine","short":"Future","main":"async fn returns a state machine; nothing runs without poll.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["async fn → Future","State machine","Laziness"],"captions":["async fn returns a value of type impl Future<Output = T>","A state machine: holds locals and the stop point, size known at compile time, no heap","Until poll is called, no line of the body runs: stricter than Python's create_task"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["async fn get() -> u32 { 5 }","let f = get();   // a Future, not run yet"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":230.0,"h":40.0,"text":"state: x, y, step 2","tone":"green","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Python:\ncreate_task starts","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Rust:\nnothing without poll","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.4,26.4]}]},{"title":"Runtime","sub":"tokio and others","short":"Runtime","main":"std has only Future; the runtime is a library.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Not in std","tokio, smol, embassy","Choice"],"captions":["In the language: async, await, Future, Poll, Context, Waker; no event loop, timers or network","tokio is the most common; async-std, smol; embassy for microcontrollers; futures for common tools","Libraries are tied to a runtime; the choice affects the whole program"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"language\nFuture, Poll","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"library\nruntime","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"tokio","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"async-std","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"smol","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"embassy","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":230.0,"h":34.0,"text":"tokio by default","tone":"yellow","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[16.4,27.6]}]},{"title":"Syntax","sub":"async and .await","short":"Syntax","main":"Postfix .await; async blocks.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["async fn",".await","async block"],"captions":["async fn get() -> String is a declaration; in Python it's async def","Waiting is postfix: fetch().await, not await fetch(); chains: req.await?.json().await?","async move { … } makes a future from code; .await only inside an async context"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"async def f():","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"async fn f()","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"await fetch()","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"fetch().await","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let f = async move {","    work().await","};"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":11.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[14.4,27.3]}]},{"title":"Combinators","sub":"gather ↔ join!","short":"Combinators","main":"Mapping: join!, spawn, JoinSet, spawn_blocking, mpsc.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["gather ↔ join!","create_task ↔ spawn","TaskGroup ↔ JoinSet"],"captions":["asyncio.gather → join! (a tuple of results), try_join! stops at the first error","create_task → spawn (returns a JoinHandle), wait_for → timeout, as_completed → FuturesUnordered","TaskGroup → JoinSet; run_in_executor → spawn_blocking; Queue → mpsc; Lock → Mutex"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let (a, b) = join!(f(1), f(2)).await;","let r = try_join!(f(1), f(2))?;"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let h = tokio::spawn(f());","let v = h.await?;"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":11.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"JoinSet","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"blocking","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"mpsc","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Mutex","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[15.4,28.7]}]},{"title":"Blocking code","sub":"spawn_blocking","short":"Blocking","main":"Don't block a worker thread; compute in a pool.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Don't block","spawn_blocking","CPU work"],"captions":["A blocking call in an async task holds a worker thread and slows other tasks","run_in_executor → tokio::task::spawn_blocking: code goes to a separate pool, result is a future","Heavy compute: rayon or plain threads; a task should reach its next .await quickly"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["async fn bad() {","    std::thread::sleep(d);   // blocks the thread","}"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let r = tokio::task::spawn_blocking(|| heavy()).await?;"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"async: waiting","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"rayon: computing","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.2,21.2]}]},{"title":"Parallelism","sub":"Work-stealing and Send","short":"Parallelism","main":"Multithreaded runtime and the Send requirement.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["One thread","Work-stealing","Send"],"captions":["asyncio: one thread, tasks never run at once: no races, but no use of cores","tokio is multithreaded by default: worker pool and work stealing; a task may change threads between .await","spawn needs Send + 'static: data held across .await moves safely between threads: no data races"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"1 thread","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k0","x":80.0,"y":100.0,"w":70.0,"h":28.0,"text":"task 1","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k1","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":70.0,"h":28.0,"text":"task 2","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k2","x":280.0,"y":100.0,"w":70.0,"h":28.0,"text":"task 3","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t0","x":60.0,"y":40.0,"w":66.0,"h":26.0,"text":"thread 1","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t1","x":140.0,"y":40.0,"w":66.0,"h":26.0,"text":"thread 2","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t2","x":220.0,"y":40.0,"w":66.0,"h":26.0,"text":"thread 3","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t3","x":300.0,"y":40.0,"w":66.0,"h":26.0,"text":"thread 4","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k0","x":50.0,"y":100.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k1","x":115.0,"y":100.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"2","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k2","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"3","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k3","x":245.0,"y":100.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"4","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k4","x":310.0,"y":100.0,"w":56.0,"h":26.0,"text":"5","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["tokio::spawn(async move { … })","// requires: Future: Send + 'static"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.1,23.4]}]},{"title":"Cancellation","sub":"drop instead of cancel","short":"Cancellation","main":"Dropping a future; cancellation safety.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["task.cancel()","drop(future)","Cancellation safety"],"captions":["Python: cancel() throws CancelledError at an await: the task can catch it and clean up","Rust: a dropped future just ceases to exist; stops at the nearest .await, Drop frees values","Cancel via select!, timeout, handle abort(); code must survive a stop between any two .await"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["t.cancel()   # CancelledError at await"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["drop(fut);   // work stopped"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"select!","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"timeout","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"abort()","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[16.6,25.1]}]},{"title":"Cost","sub":"Bytes and nanoseconds","short":"Cost","main":"Comparing overhead.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Python","Rust","Scale"],"captions":["Python coroutine: a heap object, kilobytes and microseconds per switch","tokio task: a state machine the size of its state (tens of bytes), switch in tens of nanoseconds","Hundreds of thousands of tasks and millions of connections per machine is normal for Rust"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":220.0,"h":40.0,"text":"≈ kilobytes, µs","tone":"muted","size":12.0,"